{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIntertwine"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.inv_Tw_sw_expansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.inv_Tw_sw_expansion","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionIdeal.lean#L135-L145","doc":"**`T_w⁻¹ ≠ T_{w⁻¹}` — the exact obstruction to reading the above as Mathas' 3.9.**\n\nAt a simple reflection `s = sᵢ` the group inverse is `s` itself, so `T_{s⁻¹} = T_s`.  The\nalgebra inverse is not: the quadratic relation spreads it over **two** basis elements,\n`T_s` and `T_1`.  Along a reduced word for `d` this compounds, and the resulting spread is\nprecisely the `R`-combination Mathas' statement carries. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.exists_xComp_swap'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.exists_xComp_swap'","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionIdeal.lean#L119-L133","doc":"**The mirror direction**: every `ν`-term is a single `μ`-term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.exists_xComp_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.exists_xComp_swap","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionIdeal.lean#L101-L117","doc":"**Mathas' Lemma 3.9, algebra half.**  Every `μ`-term is a *single* `ν`-term — the\nconjugating `T_d` being invertible, no `R`-combination is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.isUnit_Tw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.isUnit_Tw","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionIdeal.lean#L91-L95","doc":"**`T_w` is a unit of `H_n(q)`** whenever `q` is invertible.  `T_w` is the product of\nthe generators along a reduced word, and each generator is a unit by the quadratic\nrelation (`IwahoriHecke.isUnit_σ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.isUnit_foldl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionIdeal.isUnit_foldl","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionIdeal.lean#L83-L89","doc":"Folding generator-multiplications onto a unit keeps it a unit. ","signatureChunk":0}]}